# Footnotes with symbols and several calls to the same note (reference/components/footnote.md). Pages of 300 × 200
# with margins of 20: page area of 260 × 160 from (20, 20), which ends at y = 180. Lines of 12 (Size 10). The footnote
# area has, by default, a top margin of 8, a rule of 0.5 and a padding of 4 above its notes: 12.5 more than the notes.
#
# p1 calls iva (*) and plazo (†), and p2 calls iva again, with the same asterisk: the page has two notes, not three
# (24 + 12.5 = 36.5), and leaves 123.5 for the text. tall (90) fits after p1 and p2, up to 134; p3, which calls iva a
# third time and entrega (‡), would end at 146 and its new note needs 12 more, so it moves to page 2 with it.
# Page 1: the area, 28.5 high, at 151.5; iva at 156 and plazo at 168.
# Page 2: p3 at 20 and only entrega below, because iva is on the page of its first call: area of 16.5 at 163.5,
# entrega at 168.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: es
	Title: Prueba
	Page:
		Width: 300
		Height: 200
		Margin: 20
	Styles:
		For element: Document
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
				Size: 10
				Markup: markdown
	Section:
		Footnote number format: symbols
		Paragraph: Precio[^iva] y plazo[^plazo].
			Id: p1
		Paragraph: Portes[^iva] aparte.
			Id: p2
		Footnote:
			Id: iva
			Paragraph: IVA no incluido.
		Footnote:
			Id: plazo
			Paragraph: En días laborables.
		Block:
			Id: tall
			Box:
				Height: 90
			Break:
				Keep together: true
		Paragraph: Total[^iva] y entrega[^entrega].
			Id: p3
		Footnote:
			Id: entrega
			Paragraph: En la península.
